Subject: [PATCH 2/9] NTimeDiagonalizer: one round of the locator as a
 Turing.Round
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`qy_round`: from the locator's anchor on the layout of the rung `1^a` (`a ≤ n`) with
`(j, k) = unpair h`, one round of the locator `qyLoc κ` is a `Turing.Round` at its anchor with
the three escapes (interior, top, timeout). With `X = f a + a + 1` and `ℓ' = 2 ^ X⁴`: if
`ℓ' < n` it returns to the anchor on the layout of the rung `ℓ' + 1` and the pair
`unpair (h + 1)`, within `qyRndP` (the next rung plus polylogarithmic terms); if `n < ℓ'` it
ends at the interior or the timeout escape with the tapes off its scratch untouched; if
`ℓ' = n` at the top escape with `1^{X - 1}` on tape 4; both within `qyRndS` (linear in `n` and
the clock's budget). Assembled from the anchor's dispatch and four segments: the clocked call
(`qy_rnd_call`), the tests (`qy_rnd_tests`), the cleanup (`qy_rnd_clean`) and the pair's update
by the successor rule of `Nat.unpair` (`qy_rnd_pair`). The Implementation status paragraph
records the round.

